# .graphifyignore — controls what `/graphify` scans (syntax = .gitignore).
#
# graphify ALREADY auto-skips these by default, so they are intentionally NOT
# listed here: node_modules, .next, dist, build, out, coverage, __snapshots__,
# .turbo, .cache, .git, graphify-out, and lockfiles (pnpm-lock.yaml, etc.).
#
# Below = project-specific noise we add on top of those defaults.

# --- Generated, not hand-written source ---
src/shared/api/supabase/types.ts   # auto-generated Supabase DB types (huge, mechanical)
next-env.d.ts                       # Next.js generated ambient types

# --- Env & secrets ---
.env*

# --- Static assets (binary, no code structure to extract) ---
public/

# --- i18n message catalogs (data, not architecture) ---
messages/

# --- Tests ---
# Excluded to keep the graph focused on production code: in the last build,
# test files spawned several noise-only communities (Entity API Tests,
# Announcement Card Tests, Guild Route Tests) and many duplicate `useClient()`
# / `mock*` nodes. Delete this block if you WANT tests in the graph.
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
src/shared/lib/test/
